{
 "structure": {
  "id": "business-journey",
  "label": "Business journey",
  "groups": [
   {
    "id": "frame",
    "label": "1 · Frame",
    "order": 10,
    "description": "Which deal is this? The engagement frame, the onboarding stages and the industry profile decide what can be scoped."
   },
   {
    "id": "today",
    "label": "2 · Today",
    "order": 20,
    "description": "Where do we start? The team, its rates and its locations: the cost baseline every saving is measured against."
   },
   {
    "id": "choose-scope",
    "label": "3 · Choose the scope",
    "order": 30,
    "description": "What do we automate, and how fast? The artefacts and phases in scope, the automation potential, the adoption ramp and the eligibility gate."
   },
   {
    "id": "size",
    "label": "4 · Size the system",
    "order": 40,
    "description": "What does the agentic system cost? The run team, the token economics, the setup, the risk premium, the readiness and the knowledge hub."
   },
   {
    "id": "result",
    "label": "5 · Read the result",
    "order": 50,
    "description": "What does it return? The financial headline, the run cost, the yearly view, the results and the decision, with every read-out one click deeper."
   },
   {
    "id": "defend-present",
    "label": "6 · Defend & present",
    "order": 60,
    "description": "Is it solid, and how do we show it? The Monte Carlo, the sensitivity, the logic verification, the commercial model and the story."
   },
   {
    "id": "portfolio",
    "label": "📦 Portfolio",
    "order": 70,
    "description": "How do the products add up? Products, waves, overrides, the consolidated trajectory and the portfolio stress. Shown from two products on."
   },
   {
    "id": "reference",
    "label": "🏛️ Reference",
    "order": 80,
    "description": "Where does it come from? Architecture, glossary, dependencies, sources, the model engine and factory internals, the case files and the app configuration."
   }
  ],
